    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57470" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῑν-ητέος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be moved</i> or <i>excited</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Amat.</u>
				134a
			</span></i>; <i>to be altered</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				738d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1269a25
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κινητέον</span>, <i>one must call into
				play</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ζωγραφίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					373a
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>one must excite</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργὴν ἢ ἔλεον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					2.11
				</span></i>
			.</div>
